-- hh.rofl — WHAT THE HOUSEHOLD'S OWN RULE BOOK HOLDS in this example, as the
-- loader asserts it (examples/spat/rules.ts): the trail of each rule as facts,
-- then its clauses, every head [hh]. Written down so both engines can be held
-- to the four extension points over the same book (facts/checks.rofl, worlds
-- `spat_store` and `spat_trial`). Not read by the tool: a real book is rows
-- in the volume — `facts` for the trail, `clauses` for the AST — put there by
-- `spat rule add`, and `spat volume load` refuses a rule in a text book.
--
-- r_laptop, alex, by hand: «работа с ноутбуком — только там, где ноутбук»;
-- acme is at the office on Thursday, so defect[hh](no_laptop, acme, thu) —
-- one defect of the household's own kind, and in the trial world one more
-- reason e_schoolmv breaks Thursday
rule_by[hh](r_laptop, alex).
rule_at[hh](r_laptop, "2026-08-30T19:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_laptop, cli).
needs[hh](acme, laptop).
laptop_at[hh](home).
defect[hh](no_laptop, B, D) :- needs[hh](B, laptop), span(_, B, _, Pl, D, _, _), not laptop_at[hh](Pl).
-- r_carcheck, robin, through the bot and confirmed by her: a warning line on Friday
rule_by[hh](r_carcheck, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_carcheck, "2026-08-31T09:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_carcheck, telegram).
rule_proposed[hh](r_carcheck).
rule_confirmed[hh](r_carcheck, "2026-08-31T09:30:00+03:00", telegram).
warn[hh](car_check, "техосмотр", fri).
-- r_guest, alex: the Friday guest is not left alone at ten (no awake window
-- says so — the world only knows children), and robin is committed on Sunday
-- morning: one needs_cover row and one busy row of the household's kind. The
-- busy row is behind `deep(slots)` like every busy row, so this census does
-- not see it; demo.ts asks `free` for it.
rule_by[hh](r_guest, alex).
rule_at[hh](r_guest, "2026-08-31T10:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_guest, cli).
needs_cover[hh](guest, fri, 600).
busy[hh](robin, sun, 600).
-- r_forged, alex: a head that names main in the text — the loader stamps it
-- [hh] all the same, and may_edit[main] does not move
rule_by[hh](r_forged, alex).
rule_at[hh](r_forged, "2026-08-31T11:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_forged, cli).
may_edit[hh](nanny, c_pickup) :- person(nanny, helper).
-- r_gone, robin, retracted: its clause is not loaded at all (rules.ts), so it is not here
rule_by[hh](r_gone, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_gone, "2026-08-31T12:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_gone, cli).
rule_retracted[hh](r_gone, "2026-08-31T12:30:00+03:00", cli).
-- THE BOOK EXTENDS THE WORLD (spat.rofl §14, bridge.rofl), 2026-09-15:
-- r_gym, robin (`spat place add gym "Gym" 20 от дома` is this): a place of
-- the world from the book — place 10→11, ru_name 0→1, travel 11→12, tt 32→35
rule_by[hh](r_gym, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_gym, "2026-09-03T10:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_gym, telegram).
place[hh](gym).
ru_name[hh](gym, "Gym").
travel[hh](home, gym, 20).
-- r_shortcut, alex: the drive to school is not five minutes because a rule
-- says so — the world has travel(home, school, 20), the book's line is
-- overrides[audit](travel, k(home, school)) and never a tt; the identical
-- travel(home, sadik, 15) is neither an override nor a second row
rule_by[hh](r_shortcut, alex).
rule_at[hh](r_shortcut, "2026-09-03T11:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_shortcut, cli).
travel[hh](home, school, 5).
travel[hh](home, sadik, 15).
-- r_people, robin: a visitor is one more person of the schedule, and so are
-- robin's own required hours and a fresh constraint of hers; an adult or a
-- helper is an ACCOUNT and withheld (the guest would read every book); the
-- nanny's hours are hers to say (speaks_for); an edit's constraint is its
-- book's (key_owned); kit is the world's already (overrides), and nico as
-- the world has him is neither an override nor a second row — four
-- withheld[audit] rows, one overrides, one person and one constraint more
rule_by[hh](r_people, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_people, "2026-09-03T12:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_people, cli).
person[hh](cousin, visitor).
work_needed[hh](robin, 300).
constraint[hh](c_cousin, robin, household).
person[hh](uncle, adult).
person[hh](aunt, helper).
person[hh](kit, visitor).
person[hh](nico, child).
work_needed[hh](nanny, 300).
constraint[hh](e_skipwalk, nanny, external).
-- A NEED (spat.rofl §15, S3f 2026-09-21). r_band, robin: the band rehearses
-- every week with a guest of the world, and two conditions — the room booked
-- (alex's), and the guest able to come (his window is the confirmation).
-- This week alex put the block on Friday for both (e_band), robin sent the
-- guest's hours (e_ivanfri) and booked the room (e_bookdone): placed. Next
-- week nothing stands and the guest gave no window: blocked, no_window(ivan).
rule_by[hh](r_band, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_band, "2026-09-01T21:00:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_band, telegram).
person[hh](ivan, visitor).
ru_name[hh](ivan, "Иван").
need[hh](rehearsal, rehearsal).
ru_name[hh](rehearsal, "репетиция").
need_for[hh](rehearsal, robin).
need_for[hh](rehearsal, ivan).
need_len[hh](rehearsal, 120).
need_every[hh](rehearsal).
constraint[hh](rehearsal, robin, household).
need_req[hh](rehearsal, rehearsal_booked).
req[hh](rehearsal_booked, booked, "репточка", alex).
constraint[hh](rehearsal_booked, alex, household).
need_req[hh](rehearsal, rehearsal_ivan).
req[hh](rehearsal_ivan, confirm, "может", ivan).
constraint[hh](rehearsal_ivan, ivan, household).
-- r_party, robin: a one-off need by a date — the cake is robin's to bring,
-- nothing stands yet: open, and the reminder frame runs from Wednesday
-- (three days before Saturday 19:00): due(party_item, robin, wed 09:00)
rule_by[hh](r_party, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_party, "2026-09-01T21:05:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_party, cli).
need[hh](party, party).
need_for[hh](party, kit).
need_len[hh](party, 120).
need_by[hh](party, "2026-09-05").
need_by_on[hh](party, w0831, sat).
constraint[hh](party, robin, household).
need_req[hh](party, party_item).
req[hh](party_item, item, "торт", robin).
constraint[hh](party_item, robin, household).
-- r_noshop, robin: «закупка по пятницам» was the first week's timetable —
-- retired, so the typical line is off every week (span 48→47; w0907's moved
-- Saturday copy of it goes with it) while an added block of that name would stand
rule_by[hh](r_noshop, robin).
rule_at[hh](r_noshop, "2026-09-01T21:10:00+03:00").
rule_via[hh](r_noshop, cli).
retired[hh](shopping).
